  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-2}^{2}(3z+2)\\,\\text{d}z.$",
  "worked_solution": "Splitting up the sum and factoring out the constants, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}(3z+2)\\,\\text{d}z & =3{\\int }_{-2}^{2}z\\,\\text{d}z+2{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}{|}_{-2}^{2}+2z\\,{|}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =3(\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(-2)^{2}}{2})+2(2-(-2)) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
